Oh, that's the trick
you were talking about.

253
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,622
Thank goodness.

254
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,277
I know how to do that one.

255
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:37,360
It's risky, but I can pull it off.

256
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:40,197
Why didn't you say so from the beginning?

257
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,977
That's an easy one. All right.

258
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:45,060
In that case, do the one
with five cigarettes then.

259
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:47,001
Five cigarettes?

260
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:49,397
Hurry it up already, would you?

261
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:51,245
I want to see the trick again.

262
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,740
Why is this happening to me?

263
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:57,121
Damn that Jotaro and damn
his stupid party tricks.

264
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:02,457
But if I don't at least try to do it,
they'll really think something is up,

265
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:06,364
and they're already becoming more
suspicious of me by the minute!

266
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:07,620
And Polnareff,

267
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:11,797
loathsome idiot that he is, is seconds
away from setting off the bomb!

268
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,280
Alright, fine, dammit!

269
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:15,860
I'll do it!

270
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,500
Have it your way, five cigarettes.

271
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:29,491
That's the way, now come on, do the trick!

272
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:31,717
Alright, it's now or never.

273
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:34,877
I'm gonna do it, I'm gonna
do the trick, dammit!

274
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,360
Here goes nothing.

275
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:45,780
I did it, hot damn, I did it!

276
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:51,080
There! Did you see that? I did it!

277
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:54,260
A man can do anything when
his life is on the line.

278
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:55,650
Here.

279
00:15:55,733 --> 00:15:57,737
Last time you did this super
cool move where you drank

280
00:15:57,820 --> 00:16:00,938
a bottle of juice without
putting the cigarettes out.

281
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:07,200
Come on, drink up.

282
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,600
Oh, you blew it!

283
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,592
Jotaro, are you alright?

284
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,280
Oh my god!

285
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:21,830
Brother!

286
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,800
Brother, please! Blue bro!

287
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,534
Make that prediction go away right now!

288
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:28,080
Tear up that page!

289
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:32,119
Sorry, big bro, but the
prediction can't be changed.

290
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,137
Hurry and go back to your regular self!

291
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:38,237
If you can undo the disguise, the
real Jotaro will get blown up instead.

292
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,849
I believe in you, brother.

293
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:46,817
Jotaro, I know we've said this already,
but you're acting really weird today.

294
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:47,760
It's nothing.

295
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:50,886
I just feel a little
under the weather is all.

296
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:58,680
Crap, this couldn't get any worse.

297
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,397
I know their type.

298
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,186
Since I've put them on guard,

299
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:05,157
they're going to interrogate
me and realize I'm an imposter.

300
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,317
If they figure me out, they'll kill me.

301
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:11,753
And if I don't undo my disguise, I'll
blow up just like the prophecy said.

302
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:14,530
That's it!

303
00:17:14,613 --> 00:17:18,477
I'll just pretend I'm sick and make them
let me out of the car to relieve myself.

304
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,390
Brilliant!

305
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:24,558
Jotaro, I couldn't help but notice
the way you're clasping your hands.

306
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:26,330
Aha!

307
00:17:26,413 --> 00:17:29,017
Are you aware you've got your
left thumb on top of the others?

308
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:29,930
Well, are you?

309
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:35,100
Damn it, I wasn't prepared for this.

310
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:37,497
Does Jotaro have a weird
tick that causes him

311
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,837
to clasp his hands with
his right thumb on top?

312
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:42,400
Who even notices something like that?

313
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:43,800
What am I gonna do?

314
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:49,817
That just proves beyond a shadow of a
doubt that you are a woman in a past life.

315
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:53,037
And since unlike you, I always
put my right thumb on top,

316
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,497
it proves that I was
a man in my past life.

317
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,180
Wow, now how about that?

318
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,377
I always put my left thumb on top as well.

319
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,290
Sorry, Mr.

320
00:18:00,373 --> 00:18:03,357
Joestar, but that proves you
too were a woman in a past life.

321
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:05,616
Says you, how does it prove anything?

322
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,360
How do thumbs factor into reincarnation?

323
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,540
That's so stupid!

324
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:17,240
Now I really do feel sick.

325
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:20,480
Beast-rabbit lunatics are
driving me up the wall!

326
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:24,965
Alright, I'll tell them
I've got a stomachache.

327
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:29,377
Jotaro, what do you say we find out which
one of us can eat an orange the fastest?

328
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,290
Say what?

329
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,497
Hey, maybe you...

330
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:34,700
Stop it!

331
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,377
Don't do that, you idiot!

332
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,290
Whoa there!

333
00:18:37,373 --> 00:18:39,258
What the hell are you doing, Jotaro?

334
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:41,854
What's going on with you today, Jotaro?

335
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,140
Oh, it's nothing, guys.

336
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:47,404
But this isn't like you at all.

337
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:50,117
I just don't think it's good for
you to eat that particular orange.

338
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,657
What's the problem with it?

339
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:53,740
Well, it's obvious, isn't it?

340
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,317
Who knows where the heck
Iggy found that thing?

341
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:59,197
For all we know, he could
have dug it out of the gutter.

342
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,417
You should eat a different one.

343
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:04,277
Thanks for caring, but it doesn't look
bruised or dirty, so I think I'll be fine.

344
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:06,577
I'll eat this one, and
you can have one of those.

345
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:09,257
I can't wait to see the look
on your face when I win.

346
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:10,600
Ow! The pain!

347
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,110
Huh? Please.

348
00:19:12,193 --> 00:19:13,023
Hey, what's wrong?

349
00:19:13,106 --> 00:19:13,936
Stop the car.

350
00:19:14,019 --> 00:19:15,226
I have to go to the bathroom.

351
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,720
Come on, stop the car. Hurry!

352
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,414
Does your stomach really hurt that bad?

353
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:25,820
I can't hold it anymore!
Let me out! Let me out!

354
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,097
I'll go behind that rock!

355
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:31,640
The hospitals right there just hang
on no no going ahead without me.

356
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,348
I'll catch up once I'm done

357
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,700
Not so fast Jotaro

358
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:02,340
Take this, it's... Yes!

359
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:04,880
I did it!

360
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:06,840
I can't believe I did it!

361
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:10,568
I actually managed to get out
of that metal death trap alive!

362
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,960
I'll go behind that rock
and undo my disguise!

363
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,228
He brought up a good point.

364
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:20,237
Who knows where Iggy found this orange?

365
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:22,817
For all we know, it could
have been lying in the gutter.

366
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,400
Do you want to eat it?

367
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:26,120
Nah, you can toss it.

368
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:31,390
Success!

369
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:35,037
Now I can use K 'num's powers
to transform back to normal!

370
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:37,197
After that, they'll get
what's coming to them!

371
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:40,339
And the Dinyana Maiden
brothers will have won again!

372
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:41,600
We win!

373
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:53,480
Are you kidding me?!

374
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:00,210
Huh?

375
00:21:00,293 --> 00:21:01,572
Did you hear that sound?

376
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:02,600
Just forget it.

377
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,506
It was probably construction.

378
00:21:07,460 --> 00:21:09,280
Big bro, are you okay?

379
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:12,280
Speak to me.

380
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:14,040
Hey, little bro.

381
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:17,240
I think we lost this
battle. Bad. Really bad.

382
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:18,880
No, big brother.

383
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:21,020
No. No way.

384
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:24,535
Those wannabes haven't beaten
me and my Stan Thoth yet.

385
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:27,084
I'll destroy them all, brother.

386
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:29,040
By myself if I have to.

387
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:32,380
No, don't.

388
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,020
Don't do this brother.

389
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:39,460
These guys aren't some rookies
you can push around You'll die.

390
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:43,140
I've already decided and
I can beat them on my own.

391
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:44,560
I know I can

392
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:49,600
You were always so shy you've
really grown up little bro

393
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,640
I'm gonna kill them all.

394
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,373
What does the book of thoughts say next?

395
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,540
This is them, all right.

396
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:03,677
They're the ones who punched me and
purloined my wallet while they were at it.

397
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:04,590
All right, then.

398
00:22:04,673 --> 00:22:08,993
Beat them to a bloody pulp, and I'll
make sure you're rewarded handsomely.

399
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:10,760
It's him again!

400
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,176
I'm scared, brother.

401
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:14,085
This doesn't look good for us.

402
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:18,260
Despite his intense yet
short-lived burst of bravery,

403
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:21,257
Mondatta would have to wait a
while to avenge his brother.

404
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,620
But try not to lose heart, Mondatta.

405
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:27,200
Life is full of wonderful
ups and terrible downs.

406
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:30,530
Huh?

407
00:22:30,613 --> 00:22:32,940
Well, if it isn't Jotaro. Hm?

408
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,900
Hey, what took so long?

409
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:36,080
Forget that.

410
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:39,560
How'd you take a dump behind
that rock so fast? Huh?

411
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:41,857
I can't believe you got here before us.

412
00:22:41,940 --> 00:22:44,577
You even found time to
go to the dry cleaners.

413
00:22:44,660 --> 00:22:46,857
What the hell are you two talking about?

414
00:22:46,940 --> 00:22:48,400
Hey, it's an ambulance.

415
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:49,857
Someone must be heard.

416
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:51,800
Aw, man, that's unfortunate.

417
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:53,270
Hmm?

418
00:22:53,520 --> 00:22:54,400
Oranges, huh?

419
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:56,328
I was just getting thirsty.

420
00:22:56,840 --> 00:22:58,160
Think I'll take one.

421
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:00,090
Huh?

422
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:01,360
What's this?

423
00:23:01,620 --> 00:23:03,200
That man's clothes.

424
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,660
You recognize him?

425
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,200
Nope, can't say that I do.

426
00:23:08,780 --> 00:23:12,140
Right, let's go find out how
Avdol and Kakyoin are doing.

427
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:13,490
Huh.

428
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:16,777
And so the brothers eventually
gave up on their mission.

429
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:20,272
The battle was over, and after
all the chaos and the pain,

430
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:23,720
Jojaro and the others were
none the wiser. Ba-dum!

431
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:29,830
I believe!

432
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,310
I believe!

433
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:34,540
Oingo! Oingo! Brothers!

434
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:39,800
I can move on to Oingo!

435
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:10,617
It's a good thing. It's a good thing.

436
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:11,759
It's a good thing.

437
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,720
It's a good thing.

438
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:17,600
All of them are all up.

439
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:20,340
It's so good, right?

440
00:24:21,940 --> 00:24:24,557
You've been a good thing.

441
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:28,240
The evidence of the evidence
is that you can't be done.

442
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:33,737
The evidence of the
truth is that you can't.

443
00:24:33,820 --> 00:24:35,820
I'm so excited!

444
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:37,939
You're so excited!

445
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:39,090
That's right, right?

446
00:24:39,173 --> 00:24:41,340
Boeing-A-Boeing-A Brothers!

447
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,750
I believe it!

448
00:24:43,820 --> 00:24:44,650
I believe it!

449
00:24:45,820 --> 00:24:47,940
Boeing-A-Boeing-A Brothers!

450
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:50,311
You don't have to hit me!

451
00:24:51,260 --> 00:24:52,300
I'm so excited!

452
00:24:52,780 --> 00:24:54,140
I'm so excited!

453
00:25:03,820 --> 00:25:05,557
I think I'll hack you to
pieces while I'm on a roll.

454
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:08,140
You shall wield me, and you shall kill.

455
00:25:08,380 --> 00:25:11,909
Let's see if your Anubis stand
is all it's cracked up to be.
